=== Prompt ===
Who is Samus Aran?

=== Response ===
Samus Aran is a fictional character and the protagonist of the Metroid science fiction action-adventure video game series by Nintendo. She is one of the most recognized female characters in video games, known for her power suit and ranged combat abilities.

Samus Aran was created by Japanese video game designer and producer Gunpei Yokoi, and first appeared in the 1986 video game Metroid for the NES (Nintendo Entertainment System). She is a bounty hunter who is initially presented as a male character, but her true gender is revealed at the end of the game. This twist was designed to surprise players and challenge gender stereotypes.

Samus is known for her versatile arsenal, which includes weapons like the Morph Ball, Power Beam, Missiles, and various power-ups that enhance her abilities and weapons. She has appeared in numerous Metroid games, as well as other Nintendo titles like Super Smash Bros. and Super Metroid Amiibo figures.

In the Metroid series, Samus is a member of an intergalactic peacekeeping organization called the Galactic Federation, and she often battles various alien life forms and space pirates. Despite her tough exterior and powerful combat abilities, Samus has a softer side, as seen in her interactions with the Metroid creatures and her emotional journey throughout the games.

